# Godot CLI Verification

After any GDScript, scene (`.tscn`), or project changes, **run verification before claiming done**. Fix parse/compile errors before finishing. Do not claim success without at least headless smoke + relevant verify scripts.

## Godot binary

```bash
GODOT="/Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot"
```

Run from project root (`/Users/pbrown/Desktop/golf_incremental`).

## Required commands

**Headless smoke** (always run):

```bash
$GODOT --headless --path . --quit-after 2
```

**Import assets** (when audio, textures, or other imported assets changed):

```bash
$GODOT --headless --import --path . --quit-after 1
```

**Verify scripts** (run scripts relevant to touched systems):

```bash
$GODOT --headless --script res://tools/verify_<name>.gd
```

| Script | When to run |
|--------|-------------|
| `verify_hud_layout` | HUD / UI layout changes |
| `verify_swing_distance` | Swing / ball physics |
| `verify_upgrade_tree` | Upgrade tree / progression UI |
| `verify_upgrade_effects` | Upgrade effect logic |
| `verify_title_screen` | Title screen / main menu |
| `verify_bgm` | Background music / audio |

## Completion checklist

1. Run headless smoke; exit code must be 0.
2. Run import if assets changed.
3. Run every verify script that covers systems you touched.
4. Fix all parse/compile/runtime errors reported by the CLI.
5. Only then report the task as complete.
